.quantum/
quantum_kb/

# CSS/JS extracted from .q pages, named by content hash. Regenerated on
# every render, so a new file appears each time any page's <style> changes and
# the old one is never collected. Five got committed before this rule.
/static/styles-*.css
/static/scripts-*.js

# HTML that examples/*.q write into the repo root when run. The .q test
# suite produces these on every run, so they land in `git status` and get
# swept into unrelated commits.
/*.html

# Artifacts that examples/*.q write into the CURRENT DIRECTORY when run —
# the terminal and testing engines default their output path to
# `<name>.py` relative to cwd, so running the .q suite from the repo root
# litters it, and the files get swept into unrelated commits (twice this
# session). Ignore root-level generated .py, keeping the three real ones.
/*.py
!/compile_game.py
!/conftest.py
!/test_database.py

